              "line": 44
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "RedstoneExamples.GroundContact",
          "docstring": "    GroundContact(; h_ground = 0.0)\n\nThe ground under the aircraft: one input `h`, the altitude, and one mode,\n`contact`, false until the aircraft reaches `h_ground`. A stateless continuous\nleaf with one event, `touchdown`, a localized state event (§2.3, §10.4): the\nguard returns the sign-form value `h_ground - h`, so the step in which the\ncrossing falls ends at the crossing itself, and the handler sets `contact`. The\n`Bool` output `contact` publishes the mode from stage 1, so a `StopRequest` fed\nfrom it ends the run at the touchdown's boundary (§13.5).\n",
          "locations": [
            {
              "function": "u_types",
